{
  "acceptance": [
    {
      "check": "Group header shows avatar-mark, name, currency badge and owner-only Settings entry; summary card shows the viewer balance as hero, up to three who-owes-whom lines plus a '+N more in Balances and settle up' link whenever transfers are truncated; primary Add expense and secondary Settle up present; expense/archived/just-archived notices keep their role=status slots.",
      "how_to_verify": "Seed, sign in, open a 5+ member group with 4+ transfers at 375px and 1280px; read header, summary card and notice slots.",
      "id": "AC-1",
      "source": "IAC-1",
      "verify": "browser"
    },
    {
      "check": "Expenses, Balances and settle up, Activity and Members render as URL-driven tabs (?section=, malformed or blank defaults to expenses); Activity tab shows the 5 newest group rows with View-all linking to /activity?group=<id>; Members tab shows 5 rows with View-all to the members page; rename/archive live only in the Settings dialog, nothing settings-related on the main scroll.",
      "how_to_verify": "Click each tab, reload each tab URL directly, open Settings as owner and confirm no entry for non-owners and no settings on the scroll.",
      "id": "AC-2",
      "source": "IAC-2",
      "verify": "browser"
    },
    {
      "check": "Expenses tab lists newest-first rows (avatar left, title plus human-date metadata middle, amount right in ink with payer words 'You paid' or 'X paid' and no direction colour); search plus member/category filters sit in a disclosure that starts collapsed on phones and open inline on desktop, active filter names show on the disclosure summary, and filters survive tab switches via the URL.",
      "how_to_verify": "Add two expenses same-day out of order, set each filter, switch tabs and reload; check order, disclosure behaviour at 375px and desktop, and that filter plus tab params coexist in the URL.",
      "id": "AC-3",
      "source": "IAC-3",
      "verify": "browser"
    },
    {
      "check": "Rows expose Edit/Delete only inside an overflow menu; Delete confirms in a dialog naming the expense with a pending guard against double submit; no inline Edit link or red Delete button remains on any row.",
      "how_to_verify": "Keyboard-open the menu (Enter, Escape, focus return), delete an expense, cancel once and confirm once, double-click confirm.",
      "id": "AC-4",
      "source": "IAC-4",
      "verify": "browser"
    },
    {
      "check": "Add expense is a header button on desktop and a fixed thumb-reachable button on phones (hidden for archived groups); an empty group shows a what-to-do-first empty state with an Add-expense button; a zero-balance group shows the settled banner with zero neutral; a one-member group shows sane empty states beyond just 'no expenses'.",
      "how_to_verify": "New empty group at 375px, one-member group, settle a group to zero, open an archived group.",
      "id": "AC-5",
      "source": "IAC-5",
      "verify": "browser"
    },
    {
      "check": "Cold navigation server-renders the ledger synchronously (header, summary card, section tabs, expense rows, filter form) with skeleton blocks for the deferred Activity/Members excerpts plus the editors form fallback, and no layout shift; a failed activity read shows inline retry inside the Activity panel preserving ?section=activity; a failed main read shows a full-page error card with retry, never a half ledger; cold navigation to the expense editors paints the form fallback, never ledger content.",
      "how_to_verify": "Cold-load the group page under latency and with JS disabled (ledger paints, excerpt regions show shaped skeletons); throttle/block the activity read; break the main read; cold-load the new-expense and edit-expense routes; observe each state at 375px.",
      "id": "AC-6",
      "source": "IAC-6",
      "verify": "browser"
    },
    {
      "check": "Expense dates read as people say them computed in the viewer zone and feed times render viewer-zone relative-then-human; no UTC label appears anywhere including server HTML, no-JS render and pre-hydration paint (zone-neutral absolute first paint, viewer-zone upgrade after mount); layout holds at 375px and 1280px with no horizontal scroll; one h1, visible focus, labelled controls, reduced-motion respected.",
      "how_to_verify": "Phone plus desktop viewports, keyboard only, forced reduced-motion, JS disabled pass; compare timestamps against the viewer clock with the server in a different zone.",
      "id": "AC-7",
      "source": "IAC-7",
      "verify": "browser"
    },
    {
      "check": "formatExpenseDate covers today/yesterday/week/day-year/other-year against an explicit now (no server clock) and formatViewerTimestamp covers just-now/minutes/hours/days/absolute buckets with invalid input falling back to the raw string.",
      "how_to_verify": "Run the cases named in tests[] lib/dates.test.ts.",
      "id": "AC-8",
      "source": "IAC-7",
      "verify": "test"
    },
    {
      "check": "Excerpt Suspense fallbacks stream skeleton event/member rows (Flight fallback marker plus data-skeleton attrs), announce the wait and pulse motion-safe only; the editors boundary renders a form-shaped fallback and never ledger content; no boundary wraps the whole group segment, pinned by the absence case in tests[].",
      "how_to_verify": "Run the cases named in tests[] for the excerpt fallbacks (components/group-skeletons.test.ts) and the editors boundary (app/groups/[id]/expenses/loading.test.ts), including the whole-segment absence pin.",
      "id": "AC-9",
      "source": "IAC-6",
      "verify": "test"
    },
    {
      "check": "groupSectionFrom defaults unknown/blank values to expenses and accepts only the four closed values.",
      "how_to_verify": "Run the cases named in tests[] lib/groups/validation.test.ts.",
      "id": "AC-10",
      "source": "IAC-2",
      "verify": "test"
    },
    {
      "check": "Guard behaviour is unchanged: signed-out redirects to signin with next, stranger/malformed/missing ids 404 identically, members see the page.",
      "how_to_verify": "Signed-out fetch, cross-user fetch of another user's group, malformed id.",
      "id": "AC-11",
      "source": "TR-3",
      "verify": "browser"
    },
    {
      "check": "Every balance and transfer on the page comes from computeNetBalances plus simplifyDebts with no new arithmetic; summary hero, member rows and Balances tab agree with each other and with the members page; a departed seat holding a balance keeps its 'No longer in the group' label wherever it renders.",
      "how_to_verify": "Multi-member group with partial settle-up plus a departed seat with balance: compare hero, member balances and suggested transfers across tabs and the members page.",
      "id": "AC-12",
      "source": "TR-9",
      "verify": "browser"
    },
    {
      "check": "Activity excerpt shows the newest 5 group events with actor, action and viewer-zone time identical to the same rows on /activity; no read signature, endpoint or schema changed (group scoping is an in-page filter on ?group=, not a query change); ActivityFeed props and ActivityFeedSkeleton exports are unchanged so app/activity/loading.tsx keeps working.",
      "how_to_verify": "Produce expense/payment/member events, compare excerpt rows against /activity and /activity?group=<id>; review the diff for query/action/schema changes.",
      "id": "AC-13",
      "source": "TR-10",
      "verify": "browser"
    },
    {
      "check": "Each screen state (ideal/empty/loading/partial/error) is designed per ui.md; amounts render in group currency tabular with direction in words plus colour only where a real net is shown, zero neutral; main screen interactive under 1s.",
      "how_to_verify": "Walk empty/one/many/long-name/large-amount fixtures; time the load; check zero balances never render debt red and no expense row carries direction colour.",
      "id": "AC-14",
      "source": "TR-11",
      "verify": "browser"
    },
    {
      "check": "The non-zero-balance remove and leave refusals each carry a Settle up link to /groups/<id>?section=balances#panel-balances, and following it renders the Balances panel with its live Settle up form; no refusal link points at an anchor that does not exist on its target page.",
      "how_to_verify": "Owner plus joiner with an unpaid expense: open the members page, remove the joiner to refusal, follow the Settle up link and confirm the Balances tab with the settle form; repeat for the leave refusal.",
      "id": "AC-15",
      "verify": "browser"
    },
    {
      "check": "With JS disabled the group page paints a readable working ledger — expense rows, all four tab links, absolute zone-neutral dates with no UTC text anywhere — and the search/filter GET form filters the list; the reader is never stranded on a skeleton-only 'Loading this group…' paint.",
      "how_to_verify": "Create a group with an expense, copy the session into a javaScriptEnabled:false context, load the group page, wait 3s: rows and tabs visible, absolute date visible, Filter button submits a GET that narrows the list.",
      "id": "AC-16",
      "verify": "browser"
    }
  ],
  "alternatives_considered": [
    {
      "approach": "Client-side tab state (useState tab, all sections fetched and toggled without navigation).",
      "rejected_because": "Breaks the bookmarkable filter-URL contract, hides three sections from no-JS readers, and splits filter state across tabs; URL tabs keep every panel linkable and server-rendered."
    },
    {
      "approach": "A new per-group full activity route that the excerpt links to.",
      "rejected_because": "A new route plus reads for what /activity already shows; excerpt (newest 5, sliced in the page, no read change) plus a View-all link to /activity scoped by ?group= satisfies 'excerpt linking to the full feed' with zero new surface."
    },
    {
      "approach": "Desktop side-card layout (summary card beside the main column at 1024px, which IAC-7 permits).",
      "rejected_because": "Optional per the issue ('may'), and it doubles the loading-skeleton sync surface and the responsive QA matrix for a cosmetic gain; single centred column keeps every state trivially in sync."
    },
    {
      "approach": "Whole-page route boundary app/groups/[id]/loading.tsx for the skeleton (the v1/PR46 approach).",
      "rejected_because": "The in-repo T-14 server HTML proves the mechanism traps scriptless readers: the skeleton paints visibly while the ledger sits in a hidden Flight payload (div#S:0) that only client JS ($RC swap) reveals. Any whole-segment Suspense boundary reintroduces BUG-2 against AC-7/AC-16."
    },
    {
      "approach": "Keep the whole-page boundary and add a <noscript> style hatch that unhides the streamed payload for scriptless readers.",
      "rejected_because": "Depends on Next-internal streaming mechanics (B:0/S:0 ids, hidden-payload swap) no contract guarantees; untestable in CI, invisible until a framework upgrade renames an id, and shows both paints if the swap half-runs."
    },
    {
      "approach": "Restore the deleted #debts-heading anchor on the rewritten page so the reused refusal links resolve again.",
      "rejected_because": "The anchor would sit on the wrong tab: settling lives in the Balances panel behind ?section=balances, so a bare fragment on the expenses tab lands the reader with no settle form in view. Retargeting via one shared helper puts them on the live SettleUpForm."
    },
    {
      "approach": "Drop the scriptless requirement (AC-7/AC-16) and keep the whole-page streaming skeleton, or drop the skeleton (IAC-6) and keep scriptless.",
      "rejected_because": "That tradeoff is a scope decision for the issue author, not for this order: IAC-6 and ui.md require shaped skeleton loading states, while the URL tabs plus GET filter forms are deliberately built to work scriptless. Narrower Suspense keeps both intents — skeleton states for every deferred region, synchronous ledger for scriptless readers."
    }
  ],
  "approach": "A different attempt from a different base, not a re-roll: redo the tabbed rewrite from main (the PR46 branch is unmerged, so every step below applies to the main tree) with both QA defects designed out rather than patched. (1) Rewrite app/groups/[id]/page.tsx around URL tabs as v1 specified — breadcrumb, header (Avatar 40 + h1 + currency Badge + owner-only Settings entry), summary Card (hero viewer balance, first 3 transfer lines plus '+N more in Balances' link, settled lent-tint banner at zero, Add expense primary + Settle-up-to-balances secondary), tab nav preserving all filter params with aria-current, Expenses panel (disclosure collapsed on phones and open inline from sm: up with active-filter names on the summary, existing GET filter form + hidden section input, rows with payer Avatar, human-date meta via ExpenseDate island, ink amounts with payer words and no direction colour), Balances panel rendering <section aria-labelledby='panel-balances'><h2 id='panel-balances'> wrapping the debts Card plus the Settle up Card with the live SettleUpForm (this id is the refusal links' landing target — it must exist in this same order), Activity panel (excerpt slice(0,5) via shared ActivityRows, View-all to /activity?group=<id>, isolated try/catch with section-preserving retry), Members panel (5-row excerpt + View-all), owner Settings dialog only, fixed bottom Add-expense CTA on phones, all notice slots and the departed-seat label preserved; reuse listExpenses/listMembers/computeNetBalances/simplifyDebts/listPayments/listGroupActivity unchanged. The Activity and Members excerpts render inside in-page <Suspense> with the new ExcerptSkeleton fallbacks, so slow readers get shaped skeleton blocks with no layout shift while the ledger itself never suspends. (2) Deliberately NO app/groups/[id]/loading.tsx: a whole-segment boundary streams its fallback visibly while the resolved ledger waits in a hidden Flight payload for a JS swap that never runs scriptless (proven by the in-repo T-14 DOM), so the file itself is the BUG-2 mechanism; the absence is pinned by a unit case. (3) New components/group-skeletons.tsx with the excerpt fallbacks (event-row and member-row skeletons, data-skeleton attrs, role=status wait announcement, aria-busy, motion-safe pulse only), unit-tested in isolation per the QA environment notes. (4) New components/group-page.tsx islands (ExpenseRowMenu with focus return + Dialog delete-confirm naming the expense via deleteExpense with pending guard; GroupSettingsEntry hosting the existing rename/archive forms) and components/timestamp.tsx islands (Timestamp zone-neutral absolute first paint with viewer-zone upgrade inside time dateTime, never UTC; ExpenseDate server absolute first paint with Today/Yesterday upgrade). (5) Edit components/activity-feed.tsx to extract shared ActivityRows and render times via Timestamp; props, chips, copy, order, empty text, PreservedParams/preserved and ActivityFeedSkeleton exports untouched. (6) Edit app/activity/page.tsx for optional ?group= scope applied in the page on row.groupId (no read/signature/endpoint/schema change, default all groups, unknown scope falls back, scoped header with way back, retry and chips preserve scope via the existing preserved passthrough). (7) Edit lib/activity/queries.ts to add only the ACTIVITY_GROUP_PARAM const beside ACTIVITY_FILTER_PARAM. (8) Edit lib/groups/validation.ts for GROUP_SECTION_PARAM/GROUP_SECTIONS/groupSectionFrom. (9) Create lib/dates.ts pure presenters (explicit now, no server clock). (10) Create app/groups/[id]/expenses/loading.tsx form-shaped editors boundary. (11) Edit components/groups-panels.tsx: extract exported settleUpHref(groupId) returning `/groups/${groupId}?section=balances#panel-balances` and use it in both the remove-refusal (~line 511) and leave-refusal (~line 755) links, keeping the #48 archived branches (cannot-settle note, no link) untouched.",
  "assumptions": [
    "PGlite resolves inside the microtask queue, so skeleton fallbacks never paint locally; stream-marker plus data-skeleton unit pins per the QA environment notes are the CI proof, and QA re-checks the browser paint only where it can (editors boundary, excerpt regions under latency).",
    "The archived-group leave path already suppresses the onward link (cannot-settle note instead, per #48), so retargeting the helper affects only the non-archived refusals QA walks.",
    "QA re-runs its T-15 spec against AC-15: the old spec asserted href contains '#debts-heading', which is the defect, not the contract.",
    "Direct no-JS loads of ?section=activity or ?section=members show the sync header plus tab links with skeleton excerpt blocks (those panels suspend); the expenses default — what T-14/AC-16 assert — is fully sync."
  ],
  "confidence": 78,
  "confidence_rationale": "Both mechanisms are verified first-hand from primary sources, not inferred: the PR46 tree shows the anchor deletion with untouched hrefs, and the in-repo T-14 server HTML shows the visible skeleton plus hidden S:0 ledger plus the $RC swap script. The fixes are small relative to the rewrite (one helper, no whole-page boundary, excerpt fallbacks) and each bug carries both a unit pin and a browser criterion. What keeps this below 90: the AC-6/AC-9 mechanism rescope (region-level streaming skeletons instead of a whole-page boundary) needs reviewer sign-off, since a whole-page skeleton and a scriptless ledger cannot coexist in one route segment; and the slow-backend JS cold load loses its whole-page progress signal (recorded in residual risks).",
  "evidence": [
    "BUG-1 re-verified in-session from the trees: origin/sdlc/issue-35:app/groups/[id]/page.tsx contains 0 'debts-heading' (rewrite deleted main's <h2 id=\"debts-heading\"> at page.tsx:320) while origin/sdlc/issue-35:components/groups-panels.tsx:511,755 still render href=`/groups/${groupId}#debts-heading` — the dangle. The live target exists on the same tree at page.tsx:629 <Panel id=\"panel-balances\"> wrapping the settle Card with SettleUpForm, so ?section=balances#panel-balances resolves.",
    "BUG-2 re-verified in-session from the in-repo artifact plus the tree: qa-evidence/qa-evidence/qa-evidence/T-14-nojs-dom.html paints only the skeleton (role=status 'Loading this group…') while the 'T14 soup' row, all four tab links and the GET filter form sit inside <div hidden id=\"S:0\"> revealed only by the inline $RC('B:0','S:0') script, which never runs with JS disabled; origin/sdlc/issue-35:app/groups/[id]/loading.tsx is that boundary, and main has no such file, so the boundary itself is the defect mechanism.",
    "Scope-preservation needs no activity-feed prop change: main already carries PreservedParams/preserved (components/activity-feed.tsx:43,51,64), so AC-13 holds verbatim while retry and chips keep the group scope.",
    "QA rollup and failing specs: qa-evidence/qa-evidence/qa-report.json verdict fail with BUG-1 (T-15) minor and BUG-2 (T-14) major; T-14/T-15 repro steps in that report are the AC-15/AC-16 browser scripts."
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "Full tabbed rewrite per ui.md Group page: breadcrumb, avatar-mark header with currency badge and owner-only Settings entry, summary card with hero balance plus '+N more' overflow link, tab nav preserving filter params, redesigned expense rows (ink amounts, payer words, ExpenseDate island, overflow menus), Balances panel rendering section#panel-balances with an h2 of that id wrapping the debts Card and the Settle up Card with the live SettleUpForm (the refusal links' landing target, created in this same order), Activity/Members excerpts inside in-page Suspense with ExcerptSkeleton fallbacks, settings moved to dialog, fixed mobile CTA, full-failure error card with section-preserving retry, human dates; reuse listExpenses/listMembers/computeNetBalances/simplifyDebts/listPayments/listGroupActivity unchanged; all notice slots and the departed-seat label preserved. No #debts-heading is restored: settling lives behind ?section=balances.",
      "path": "app/groups/[id]/page.tsx",
      "why": "The screen the issue rebuilds; all IAC-1..7 land here, and the Balances target the fixed refusal links land on must be created by the same order."
    },
    {
      "action": "create",
      "change": "Client islands: ExpenseRowMenu (overflow menu with Edit link and Dialog delete-confirm naming the expense via deleteExpense + ConfirmStep with pending guard) and GroupSettingsEntry (Settings button opening Dialog hosting existing rename/archive forms); timestamps deliberately not here.",
      "path": "components/group-page.tsx",
      "why": "IAC-4 overflow actions and IAC-2 settings-behind-entry need client behaviour the server page cannot render."
    },
    {
      "action": "create",
      "change": "Neutral client time islands: Timestamp (zone-neutral absolute first paint, effect upgrade to viewer-zone relative+absolute inside time dateTime, never a UTC label) and ExpenseDate (server absolute first paint, viewer-zone Today/Yesterday upgrade); shared by group page, feed and /activity.",
      "path": "components/timestamp.tsx",
      "why": "IAC-7 viewer-zone times without the banned UTC first paint and without making a screen module a dependency of shared code."
    },
    {
      "action": "create",
      "change": "Excerpt Suspense fallbacks: ActivityExcerptSkeleton (event rows shaped like ActivityRowItem) and MembersExcerptSkeleton (member rows shaped like the roster rows), each with data-skeleton attrs, role=status wait announcement, aria-busy and motion-safe pulse only; no summary/tabs/expense-row markup, so they can never be mistaken for the ledger.",
      "path": "components/group-skeletons.tsx",
      "why": "IAC-6 shaped skeleton states without a whole-page boundary: deferred excerpt regions stream skeleton blocks with no layout shift while the ledger stays synchronously server-rendered for scriptless readers."
    },
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "Extract shared ActivityRows list used by ActivityFeed and the group excerpt; render row timestamps through Timestamp. Props, chips, copy, order, empty text, PreservedParams/preserved and ActivityFeedSkeleton exports unchanged so /activity and its skeleton cannot break.",
      "path": "components/activity-feed.tsx",
      "why": "The excerpt must reuse the feed rendering (contract face) without duplicating row markup; timestamps must move to the viewer zone per IAC-7."
    },
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "Accept optional ?group= to scope the feed to one group (filter applied in the page on row.groupId, no read/signature/endpoint/schema change, default all groups, unknown scope falls back to the whole feed with chips intact); scoped header names the group with a way back to every group; retry and chips preserve filter and group params via the existing preserved passthrough; render through the shared rows so times are zone-correct.",
      "path": "app/activity/page.tsx",
      "why": "The group excerpt's View-all target must preserve group scope; this page's rendered output also changes via Timestamp so it must be named."
    },
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "Add only the ACTIVITY_GROUP_PARAM const ('group') beside ACTIVITY_FILTER_PARAM with a comment recording it is a page-level filter, not a read: scoping narrows already-read rows by row.groupId, so no query, endpoint or index changes.",
      "path": "lib/activity/queries.ts",
      "why": "The page that writes the ?group= link and the page that reads it must share one spelling; the const lives beside the filter key so it cannot drift."
    },
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "Add GROUP_SECTION_PARAM, GROUP_SECTIONS closed set and groupSectionFrom parser (unknown/blank defaults to expenses) beside the existing filter-param pattern.",
      "path": "lib/groups/validation.ts",
      "why": "Tab state lives in the URL like the existing filters, so parser and key live with the other boundary constants and cannot drift."
    },
    {
      "action": "create",
      "change": "Pure date presenters with no clock of their own: formatExpenseDate for YYYY-MM-DD against an explicit today string to Today/Yesterday/weekday/3 Oct/3 Oct 2025, and formatViewerTimestamp for relative bucket plus local-zone absolute with raw-string fallback. No backend branch, no timezone input needed.",
      "path": "lib/dates.ts",
      "why": "IAC-7 human dates; relative labels are decided with a viewer-supplied day so the server clock can never mislabel them."
    },
    {
      "action": "create",
      "change": "Minimal editor-shaped loading boundary (form skeleton, never the group summary/tabs/rows) covering the new-expense and edit-expense segments so the editors keep a designed loading state with an announced, motion-safe wait.",
      "path": "app/groups/[id]/expenses/loading.tsx",
      "why": "Editors are JS-gated forms that need their own fallback; with no group-level boundary this file is the route-level skeleton that remains."
    },
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "Extract an exported settleUpHref(groupId) helper returning `/groups/${groupId}?section=balances#panel-balances` and use it for both the remove-refusal link (~line 511) and the leave-refusal link (~line 755), replacing the `/groups/${groupId}#debts-heading` hrefs that dangle once the rewrite deletes that heading; keep the #48 archived branches (cannot-settle note, no link) untouched.",
      "path": "components/groups-panels.tsx",
      "why": "BUG-1 fix: both refusals must land on the live Balances settle target created in this same order; a shared helper keeps the two call sites from drifting apart again and makes the target unit-pinnable."
    }
  ],
  "issue": 35,
  "kind": "feature",
  "mode": "committed",
  "out_of_scope": [
    "Expense editor form internals and settle-up sheet internals (next piece): SettleUpForm/DeletePaymentForm render unchanged inside the Balances tab.",
    "Balance math, simplification, filter semantics and activity-writing changes: no split, balance, simplify or feed-writer code is touched; ?group= filters already-read rows in the page.",
    "Dark mode: tokens stay light-only per ui.md.",
    "Approved docs and framework paths (.sdlc/**, docs/**, .github/**): untouched; no ADR is recorded by this plan.",
    "A separate per-group full activity route: group scoping stays a ?group= filter on /activity.",
    "Desktop side-card summary layout: single centred column kept (IAC-7 allows either).",
    "The pre-existing app/groups/[id]/members/loading.tsx boundary: same Suspense shape, but it predates this issue, sits outside this issue's criteria, and QA never walks the members route scriptless; flagged in risks instead."
  ],
  "qa_script": [
    "Seed and sign in as two users in different zones; open a group with several expenses, payments and member events.",
    "At 375px and 1280px: header, hero balance, transfer lines plus '+N more' link, Add expense (fixed bottom button on phone, header button on desktop), Settle up jumps to the Balances tab with the live settle form.",
    "Switch all four tabs; reload each tab URL directly; try malformed ?section=; set expense filters then switch tabs and confirm filters survive.",
    "Keyboard only: tab bar, filter disclosure, overflow menu open/Edit/Escape/Delete confirm with focus return, Settings dialog open/close.",
    "Owner plus joiner with an unpaid expense: members page, remove the joiner to refusal, follow the Settle up link to ?section=balances#panel-balances and confirm the live settle form; repeat for the leave refusal.",
    "No-JS context with the session cookies: group page shows expense rows, all four tab links and an absolute date with no UTC text and no 'Loading this group…'-only paint; submit the Filter GET and confirm the list narrows.",
    "Regression sweep: editors cold-load shows the form fallback (never ledger rows); archived groups stay read-only with no Add links; delete one expense via the overflow menu (cancel once, confirm once)."
  ],
  "reproduced": true,
  "residual_risks": [
    "Against real Neon latency the ledger region paints blank until the server responds instead of a skeleton; the deferred excerpts and the editors keep shaped skeleton states, and PGlite resolves too fast for any of this to be observable locally — but a slow-backend JS cold load loses its whole-page progress signal.",
    "A direct scriptless load of ?section=activity or ?section=members shows the sync header plus tab links with skeleton excerpt blocks (those panels suspend by design); the expenses default asserted by T-14/AC-16 is fully synchronous.",
    "The ?group= scoping on /activity is a product judgment (scoped by default from a group entry, unscoped feed one click away); review may prefer the unfiltered landing."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "If a later rewrite renames Panel ids, the refusal links dangle again — the shared settleUpHref helper plus its unit pin turn that into a test failure, not a silent QA find.",
    "The delete-confirm question sentence is duplicated between DeleteExpenseForm (edit page) and the row menu confirm; a future copy change must touch both — flagged here rather than refactored, to avoid changing the edit page caller.",
    "A departed seat with a balance renders in balance/transfer lists but has no member row in the Members excerpt; the excerpt links to the members page where it is labelled, pinned in AC-12 rather than special-cased here.",
    "Icon export names are verified at build time; if the installed lucide-react has removed the MoreVertical alias, use the current vertical-ellipsis export with identical placement and size.",
